      "writtenOn": "2017-11-23T06:13:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re: Calin. Thanks. I already fixed ag/3252125. :)\nRe: Todd. Strictly speaking, anything other than directly checking the existence of /vendor/lib in the default search path is incorrect or more verbose than this. We do have \u0027ro.treble.enabled\u0027 but that is not appropriate because we may or may not have vendor/lib in treble-ized devices. Specifically, vendor apk is should be treated as unbunded when following conditions are all met.\n\n1) device is treble-ized. (ro.treble.enabled \u003d\u003d true)\n2) platform is P or later (ro.build.version.release \u003e\u003d P)\n3) the device is not an upgrading device (launched in P or later) (ro.product.first_api_level \u003e\u003d ??. ?? is because we don\u0027t know the API level of P yet).",
      "parentUuid": "36be5130_0b91879e",
